  "id": "Compound::DB00692 - Gene::152",
  "verbalization": "Phentolamine, a selective alpha-1 adrenergic receptor antagonist, is shown to bind to Adra1d, a subunit of the alpha-adrenergic receptor, which in turn participates in alpha-adrenergic receptor activity. This pathway leads to the participation of Adra2c in adrenergic receptor activity, suggesting a potential role for Phentolamine in modulating Adra2c function. The evidence from the three paths collectively supports a mechanism where Phentolamine interacts with Adra1d, influencing the activity of Adra2c through the alpha-adrenergic receptor pathway. The consistent binding to Adra1d across all three paths, along with the shared participation in receptor activity, indicates a plausible mechanism of action. The integration of these pathways highlights the involvement of Adra2c in adrenergic signaling, and the presence of a well-defined binding interaction with Adra1d suggests that Phentolamine may exert its effects through this specific receptor-subunit interaction. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Phentolamine and Adra2c, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct impact on Adra2c function.",
